{"run":"m5-pinned-dev-C1-pilot","kind":"experiment-summary","markdown":["Drop signals (drop-signals.mjs), chrome, load idle, plan t14-late: 2 drags.","","Never-take rules, read at the start point before the press: a rule predicts that the drag never takes, and a prediction whose drag took (`XdndSelection`) is a false negative; \"after the path\" are the false negatives whose take came after the path's end, the drags a skipped hold would lose. A load's counts stand for an adoption only from 300 drags.","","| load | rule | drags | predicted never | false negatives | of them after the path | true negatives | cells of the false negatives |","|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|","| idle | role:range | 2 (under 300) | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | – |","| idle | role:text | 2 (under 300) | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | – |","| idle | role:canvas | 2 (under 300) | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | – |","| idle | role:any | 2 (under 300) | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | – |","| idle | role:any-hit-chain | 2 (under 300) | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | – |","| idle | xdnd-aware | 2 (under 300) | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | – |","","After the release, for drags whose source took by the release: a signal says the drop landed (positive) or not. Activation: Chrome's own `_NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW` request for its window within 300 ms of the release. Accept cursor: the accept rule's cursor (accept.rs) shown at the release, indeterminate where a change the records cannot order against the release would decide it (`acceptAtRelease`). A false negative calls a landed drop lost; a false positive calls a lost drop landed, the one that would let a drag answer success wrongly. The counts of true and false are of the determinate drags; \"false positives, indeterminates counted\" counts every indeterminate leave as a false positive, which is the count that stands against a bar.","","| load | signal | drags | drops | leaves | true positives | false negatives | false positives | true negatives | indeterminate drops / leaves | false positives, indeterminates counted | drop latency p50 / p95 / max (ms) |","|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|---|","","The release at the accept (measurement only, `--drag-dnd-release-at-accept`): after a take the path keeps its own pacing and the release comes at the accept rule's cursor change, the 350 ms floor its ceiling. A false release is a drag released at the accept whose drop did not land into the zone; on `nozone`, a drag bound to leave, any accept read is a false accept.","","| load | lane | cell | drags | released at the accept | false releases | at the ceiling | of them not landed | accept after the take p50 / p95 / max (ms) | answer median (ms) |","|---|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|","","Late takes (#264): the source took `XdndSelection` only after the release, which no engine of today watches for in front. \"Answered ok\": the drag answered success all the same; \"landed\": its drop counted anyway.","","| load | lane | cell | drags | took | late takes | answered ok | landed | take after the release p50 / max (ms) |","|---|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|","| idle | cua | freeze-250 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 0 | 0.9 / 1.5 |","","Covered paths on the background route (measurement only, `--drag-ignore-cover`), shared mode, Chrome raised but not active: a window over a part of the path, either an override-redirect window of the harness's (`cua:cover`) or the harness's managed front window, its frame and title bar included (`cua:cover-managed`). A kind survived when its effect showed (a drop source: when Chrome took `XdndSelection`; the engine then cancels the drop, since Chrome is not in front). The start role is the role probe's at the path's first point.","","| cell | covered part | cover | drags | survived | start role |","|---|---|---|---:|---:|---|","","T14's Chrome cells (drop-signals-judge.mjs `chromeDropVerdict`), plan t14-late, load idle:","","| lane | cell | drags | never took | landed | ok, nothing pending | unconfirmed | late takes | reported | false ok | false releases (answered ok) | harness Escapes |","|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|","| cua | freeze-250 | 2 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 2 | 2 | 0 | 0 (0) | 0 |","","Every late take reported, no false ok, no missing landing, every notice refused once; every cell of the plan ran.","","Findings (counted, not fails): 2 late takes, 2 reported; T14's share, reported and not a fail: 0 of 0 landed drops answered unconfirmed, within 5%.",""],"complete":true,"failed":[],"desktop":{"active_start":{"id":8388620,"owner":"foreign"},"active_end":{"id":8388620,"owner":"foreign"},"holder":14680076,"skipped":[],"trace":{"clean":true,"requests":347,"mutating":30,"foreign":[],"unplaced":0},"watchdog":{"state":"ended","round_trips":12},"chrome":{"spawned":1,"terminated":[],"killed":[],"left":[]},"session":{"address":"unix:path=/tmp/cua171-run-GLDzm9/session/bus/dbus-8sdubwDVu4,guid=d61da831218ad4a6d72c66b36afd1f35","a11y":"unix:path=/run/user/501/at-spi/bus_1,guid=90fd2083f92d1011a44d93ba6afd1f35","terminated":true,"killed":false},"leftovers":{"roots":["/tmp"],"dirs":[],"buses":[],"clear":true},"record":{"skipped":"the display is a private one, and the run's caller declined to start the whole-run RECORD on it"}},"finished":"2026-11-18T03:45:15.535Z","gate":"pinned-dev","label":"development run on the pinned release, not acceptance, never counted"}
